{
  "id": "spr_wispook",
  "kind": "object",
  "type": "sprite",
  "name": "Wispook sprite",
  "notes": "Wispook, a floating lilac ghost with big dark eyes, little arms and a scalloped wispy hem, drawn in the style of the monsters that walk around in GBA monster games: dark closed outline, 3 shades lit from the top-left, eyes with a glint. Seen from 8 directions: the front (down), the back (up), the side (right), the three-quarter views (down-right: the face turned right; up-right: the back turned right) and their left versions. The left views are drawn on their own, not mirrored by the engine: the shapes and the face mirror, but the shading stays lit from the top-left like every other view. Each view has a standing frame, a breathing frame (1 px lower), a blink, the frames it floats (bobs 1 px up and down) with, and an attack lunge. Every frame stays inside the 16x16 box with its outline closed, so nothing is ever cut at the edges. Too many frames to keep whole in video memory: it streams (only the frames on screen are loaded).",
